## Section B: Candidate Improvement Priorities & Criterion-by-Criterion Scoring

### Scoring System & Weighting Methodology
Each priority is scored from **1 to 5** across six criteria. To produce a **Composite Priority Score out of 100**, the raw criterion scores are weighted according to frontline operational and NHS strategic priorities:

$$\text{Composite Score} = (C1 \times 4) + (C2 \times 4) + (C3 \times 3) + (C4 \times 3) + (C5 \times 3) + (C6 \times 3)$$

- **C1: Magnitude of Winter Problem** (Weight: 20%, Max 20 pts)
- **C2: Strength of Supporting Evidence** (Weight: 20%, Max 20 pts)
- **C3: Cost-Effectiveness** (Weight: 15%, Max 15 pts)
- **C4: Alignment with NHS Plan & UK Life Sciences Strategy** (Weight: 15%, Max 15 pts)
- **C5: Multi-Timeframe Impact (1–3y, 3–5y, 5–10y)** (Weight: 15%, Max 15 pts)
- **C6: Impact on Reducing Health Inequalities** (Weight: 15%, Max 15 pts)

